=begin
  unstash.lic

  The opposite of ;stash. Opens your vault at your hometown's Carousel
  (Crossing: ;go2 8285, through an arch, PULL LEVER, GO DOOR, OPEN VAULT),
  gets back what ;stash wrote down, and puts each thing back in the container
  it came from (or your crafting_container if that doesn't work). Then it
  closes the vault and leaves you in the Carousel.

  Only things ;stash wrote down come back, so whatever else you keep in the
  vault stays there. Each item's full name is checked when you pick it up. If
  it's the wrong one, it goes back and stays on the list.

  Weapons go back the way combat-trainer puts them away after a hunt: worn
  again if your standard gear set wears them, else on their harness, in
  their container, or stowed.

  If the vault doesn't know an item by the name ;stash wrote down (GET MANA
  FOUNT doesn't work), it tries just the noun (GET FOUNT), still checking the
  full name. Anything that isn't there anymore is dropped from the list. If there's no
  room to put something away, the rest stays in the vault and on the list for
  next time.

  ;stash writes down what each thing is for, so you can get back part of it.
  Crafting materials (ingots, deeds, cloth and the like) are heavy, so they
  only come back when you ask for materials, or for everything.

  ;unstash crafting <discipline> is for t2: each crafting block starts with
  it and ends with ;stash crafting <discipline>, so the work orders have
  their logbook and tools even when a hunt was stopped before it got the
  crafting gear back (2026-11-11: both Enchanting blocks failed with the
  enchanting logbook in the vault). It's the same as ;unstash <discipline>:
  tools only. Tools and materials stay separate, since carrying the
  materials too is too much to lug around; rare ones like a massive selatila
  shard would come along for nothing.

  Usage:
    ;unstash                    # everything, materials too
    ;unstash crafting           # all crafting gear, no materials
    ;unstash crafting forging   # the same as ;unstash forging (shaping, enchanting, outfitting, alchemy too): t2's crafting blocks start with it
    ;unstash forging            # just forging gear, no materials
    ;unstash shaping            # just shaping gear, no materials
    ;unstash enchanting         # just enchanting gear, no materials
    ;unstash outfitting         # just outfitting gear, no materials
    ;unstash alchemy            # just alchemy gear
    ;unstash materials          # just the crafting materials
    ;unstash materials forging  # just forging's materials (or shaping, and so on)
    ;unstash marathon           # before ;taskmaster marathon: outfitting gear, plus the burlap cloth,
                                #   rat-pelt leather, wool yarn and cotton thread it sews and knits from
                                #   (not the rare cloths and leathers), so the marathon doesn't buy them again
    ;unstash weapons            # just your weapons, back where combat-trainer keeps them
    ;unstash extras             # just your extras
=end

# What's stashed right now, written by ;stash
STASH_LIST = File.join(DATA_DIR, XMLData.game, Char.name, 'stash.yaml')

# What ;stash says each thing is for
CRAFTING = %w[forging shaping enchanting outfitting alchemy].freeze
GROUPS = (CRAFTING + %w[weapons extras]).freeze

# ;unstash marathon: the stock ;taskmaster marathon sews and knits from,
# which comes back with the outfitting tools. The marathon tops up what you
# carry, so stock left in the vault was bought again (2026-11-18). Only these
# four: rare cloths and leathers stay in the vault.
MARATHON_STOCK = /\b(?:burlap cloth|rat-pelt leather|wool yarn|cotton thread)$/i

# How many times one name is asked for while it keeps handing over other
# things of yours this unstash also wants
MAX_TRIES = 20

# Getting in and out of the vault: the same steps and messages as ;stash
ARCHES = ['go blackwood arch', 'go ironwood arch', 'go rosewood arch'].freeze
ARCH_IN = /escorts you through/
RENT_DUE = /\brent\b/i
ARCH_RESTRICTED = /access to that arch is restricted/
ARCH_BUSY = /is using that booth|blocks|someone|using|Sorry/
LEVER_PULLED = /door pops open/
VAULT_OPENED = [/^The vault opens/, /already open/i].freeze
CHAMBER = /Chamber/
# Where you may be already, as ;trash-sort leaves you. The map doesn't know
# these rooms, so walking to the Carousel from them fails ("DRCT: Unable to
# resolve the current room", 2026-11-22).
CAROUSEL_CHAMBER = /Carousel Chamber/
CAROUSEL_BOOTH = /Carousel Booth/

# bput returns only the matched text, so match the whole line to check the item name
GET_SUCCESS = [/^You get .*/, /^You pick up .*/].freeze
GET_MISSING = [/^What were you referring to/, /^I could not find/].freeze
NOT_FOUND = [/^What were you referring to/, /^I could not find/, /^I don't know what you are referring to/].freeze

def load_stash_list
  File.exist?(STASH_LIST) ? YAML.safe_load(File.read(STASH_LIST)) || [] : []
end

def save_stash_list(entries)
  FileUtils.mkdir_p(File.dirname(STASH_LIST))
  File.write(STASH_LIST, entries.to_yaml)
end

def hands_empty?
  DRC.right_hand.nil? && DRC.left_hand.nil?
end

# The hand display and room title can lag the game text by a moment
def settle
  10.times do
    return true if yield

    pause 0.1
  end
  false
end

def in_room?(pattern)
  [XMLData.room_title, XMLData.room_name].any? { |title| title.to_s =~ pattern }
end

def in_chamber?
  in_room?(CHAMBER)
end

# Walks to the hometown's Carousel and opens your vault, starting from the
# chamber or a booth if you're in one already. Remembers how far it got in
# @vault_steps so leave_vault can undo it. Says why and returns false if it
# can't.
def open_vault(settings)
  @vault_steps = []
  if in_room?(CAROUSEL_CHAMBER)
    # Already in, maybe with the vault open ("That is already open.")
    @vault_steps.push(:booth, :chamber)
  else
    return false unless into_booth(settings)
    return false unless into_chamber
  end

  result = DRC.bput('open vault', *VAULT_OPENED, RENT_DUE, *NOT_FOUND, /^You can't/)
  unless VAULT_OPENED.any? { |pattern| result =~ pattern }
    DRC.message("unstash: the vault didn't open: #{result.empty? ? 'no reply' : result}")
    return false
  end
  @vault_steps << :open
  true
end

# To the hometown's Carousel and through an arch, unless you're in a booth
# already
def into_booth(settings)
  if in_room?(CAROUSEL_BOOTH)
    @vault_steps << :booth
    return true
  end

  room = get_data('town')[settings.hometown]&.dig('vault', 'id')
  unless room
    DRC.message("unstash: no vault listed for your hometown, #{settings.hometown}.")
    return false
  end
  unless DRCT.walk_to(room)
    DRC.message("unstash: couldn't walk to the Carousel (room #{room}).")
    return false
  end
  enter_booth
end

# From the booth through its door into the vault chamber
def into_chamber
  unless DRC.bput('pull lever', LEVER_PULLED, *NOT_FOUND, /^You can't/) =~ LEVER_PULLED
    DRC.message("unstash: pulling the lever didn't open the door.")
    return false
  end

  DRC.bput('go door', /.+/)
  unless settle { in_chamber? }
    DRC.message("unstash: GO DOOR didn't reach the Carousel Chamber. Room: #{XMLData.room_title.inspect}")
    return false
  end
  @vault_steps << :chamber
  true
end

# Through the first arch whose booth is free, waiting a while if all are in use
def enter_booth
  6.times do
    ARCHES.each do |arch|
      result = DRC.bput(arch, ARCH_IN, RENT_DUE, ARCH_RESTRICTED, ARCH_BUSY, *NOT_FOUND)
      if result =~ ARCH_IN
        @vault_steps << :booth
        return true
      end
      if result =~ RENT_DUE
        DRC.message('unstash: vault rent is due. Pay it at the Carousel desk (GO DESK), then try again.')
        return false
      end
      # Not in the Carousel any more (say, someone went through an arch by hand)
      if NOT_FOUND.any? { |pattern| result =~ pattern }
        DRC.message("unstash: there's no #{arch.split[1]} arch here, so stopping.")
        return false
      end
    end
    DRC.message('unstash: every booth is busy. Waiting 10 seconds.')
    pause 10
  end
  DRC.message('unstash: gave up waiting for a free booth.')
  false
end

# Closes the vault and goes back out to the Carousel, as far as open_vault got
def leave_vault
  steps = @vault_steps.to_a
  DRC.bput('close vault', /^You close the vault/, /already closed/i, /isn't open/i, *NOT_FOUND) if steps.include?(:open)
  DRC.bput('go door', /.+/) if steps.include?(:chamber)
  DRC.bput('go arch', /door slams closed/, /.+/) if steps.include?(:booth)
  @vault_steps = []
end

# The GET line names this exact item, e.g. "You get some muracite tongs from
# ..." and not "You get some muracite tongs with icesteel clamps from ...".
def right_item?(result, name)
  return true if name.nil?

  result =~ /^You (?:get|pick up) (?:a|an|some|the|your) #{Regexp.escape(name)} (?:from|off)\b/
end

def put_back(item)
  DRC.bput("put my #{item} in vault", /^You put/, *NOT_FOUND, /no room/i, /^You can't/)
  return true if settle { hands_empty? }

  DRC.message("unstash: couldn't put #{item} back in the vault. It's still in your hand.")
  exit
end

def get_from_vault(item)
  DRC.bput("get #{item} from vault", *GET_SUCCESS, *GET_MISSING, *DRCI::GET_ITEM_FAILURE_PATTERNS)
end

# The ways to ask the vault for something: the name ;stash wrote down, then
# (with a full name) each other word of it with the noun, then the bare noun.
# The word before the noun isn't always one GET takes: GET MANA FOUNT says
# "What were you referring to?" for a fragile rough mana fount, so two of
# them were left in the vault and dropped from the list (2026-11-08 and
# 11-09). And a cloth stashed as THIN CLOTH ("thin Imperial weave cloth",
# 2026-11-18) can find another thin cloth first. The name check in fetch makes
# sure what comes out is ours.
#
# The marathon's four stocks are just their full names: GET takes those, so
# if it finds nothing they're gone. The bare noun would find a rare leather
# or cloth instead, and the entry would stay on the list for good (6 rat-pelt
# leathers listed with 3 in the vault, 2026-11-25).
def vault_addresses(item, name)
  return [item] if name.nil? || (item == name && name.match?(MARATHON_STOCK))

  words = name.split
  noun = words.last
  ([item] + words[0...-1].reverse.map { |word| "#{word} #{noun}" } + [noun]).uniq
end

# Returns :got, :missing, :wrong, :failed, or :container_full. :missing (it's
# dropped from the list) only when no way of asking found anything at all.
#
# One name can fit several of your things: PEWTER BAR is the tiny bar and the
# huge one, THIN CLOTH three of the cloths. When GET hands over one of the
# others this unstash wants too, it goes home as that one (the block hears
# which, to take it off the list) and the same name is asked again, so the
# vault empties out instead of putting it back and giving up.
def fetch(entry, container, others = [])
  item, name = entry.values_at('item', 'name')
  wrong = false
  vault_addresses(item, name).each do |address|
    MAX_TRIES.times do
      result = get_from_vault(address)
      break if GET_MISSING.any? { |pattern| result =~ pattern }
      return :failed unless settle { !hands_empty? }

      if right_item?(result, name)
        return :got if entry['from'] == 'gear' ? return_weapon? : DRCI.put_away_item?(address, [entry['from'], container].compact.uniq)

        put_back(address)
        return :container_full
      end

      other = others.find { |candidate| right_item?(result, candidate['name']) }
      unless other
        put_back(address)
        wrong = true
        break
      end
      unless DRCI.put_away_item?(address, [other['from'], container].compact.uniq)
        put_back(address)
        return :container_full
      end
      others.delete_if { |candidate| candidate.equal?(other) }
      yield other if block_given?
    end
  end
  wrong ? :wrong : :missing
end

# A weapon ;stash weapons took, put back the way combat-trainer does after a
# hunt (EquipmentManager): worn again if your standard gear set wears it,
# else on its harness, in its container, or stowed
def return_weapon?
  @equipment ||= EquipmentManager.new
  @equipment.return_held_gear && settle { hands_empty? }
end

# A crafting material ;stash took (it marks them), not gear
def material?(entry)
  entry['kind'] == 'materials'
end

# groups nil means everything, materials and anything stashed before ;stash
# wrote down what it's for. Otherwise the entry has to be for one of the
# groups, and be a material if materials is true, or not one if it's false.
# materials can also be a pattern (;unstash marathon): the gear, plus only the
# materials whose name matches it.
def wanted?(entry, groups, materials)
  return true if groups.nil?
  return false unless (entry['for'].to_a & groups).any?
  return !material?(entry) || entry['name'].to_s.match?(materials) if materials.is_a?(Regexp)

  material?(entry) == materials
end

asked_for = Script.current.vars[1].to_s.downcase
which = Script.current.vars[2].to_s.downcase
groups, materials = case asked_for
                    when '', 'all' then [nil, nil]
                    when 'crafting'
                      if which.empty? then [CRAFTING, false]
                      # One discipline's gear, no materials, for a t2 crafting block
                      elsif CRAFTING.include?(which) then [[which], false]
                      else
                        DRC.message("unstash: use ;unstash crafting, or ;unstash crafting #{CRAFTING.join(', ')}.")
                        exit
                      end
                    when 'materials', 'material'
                      if which.empty? then [CRAFTING, true]
                      elsif CRAFTING.include?(which) then [[which], true]
                      else
                        DRC.message("unstash: use ;unstash materials, or ;unstash materials #{CRAFTING.join(', ')}.")
                        exit
                      end
                    # Outfitting gear and the marathon's stock, before ;taskmaster marathon
                    when 'marathon' then [['outfitting'], MARATHON_STOCK]
                    when *GROUPS then [[asked_for], false]
                    else
                      DRC.message('unstash: use ;unstash for everything, or ;unstash forging, shaping, enchanting, outfitting, alchemy, ' \
                                  'crafting, materials, marathon, weapons or extras.')
                      exit
                    end

stash_list = load_stash_list
if stash_list.empty?
  DRC.message('unstash: nothing is stashed right now.')
  exit
end

if stash_list.none? { |entry| wanted?(entry, groups, materials) }
  DRC.message("unstash: nothing for #{[asked_for, which].reject(&:empty?).join(' ')} is stashed right now. ;stash list shows what is.")
  exit
end

unless hands_empty?
  DRC.message('unstash: empty your hands first.')
  exit
end

settings = get_settings
container = settings.crafting_container
results = Hash.new { |hash, result| hash[result] = [] }

begin
  exit unless open_vault(settings)

  # Newest first. An entry can come back while another one is being asked for
  # (fetch), so they're tracked by which object they are, not where in the list.
  pending = stash_list.select { |entry| wanted?(entry, groups, materials) }.reverse
  done = []
  forget = lambda do |gone|
    done << gone
    stash_list.delete_if { |listed| listed.equal?(gone) }
    save_stash_list(stash_list)
  end
  pending.each do |entry|
    next if done.any? { |gone| gone.equal?(entry) }

    # Others this one's name might hand over: named ones, not weapons
    others = pending.reject do |other|
      other.equal?(entry) || done.any? { |gone| gone.equal?(other) } || other['name'].nil? || other['from'] == 'gear'
    end
    result = fetch(entry, container, others) do |other|
      results[:got] << other['name']
      forget.call(other)
    end
    results[result] << (entry['name'] || entry['item'])
    break if result == :container_full
    next unless %i[got missing].include?(result)

    forget.call(entry)
  end
ensure
  leave_vault
end

DRC.message("unstash: got back: #{results[:got].join(', ')}") unless results[:got].empty?
DRC.message("unstash: not in the vault anymore, dropped from the list: #{results[:missing].join(', ')}") unless results[:missing].empty?
DRC.message("unstash: found something else first, left it and kept on the list: #{results[:wrong].join(', ')}") unless results[:wrong].empty?
DRC.message("unstash: couldn't pick up, kept on the list: #{results[:failed].join(', ')}") unless results[:failed].empty?
DRC.message("unstash: no room to put #{results[:container_full].first} away. #{stash_list.count { |entry| wanted?(entry, groups, materials) }} item(s) still in the vault and on the list.") unless results[:container_full].empty?
